<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024- exam 25</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024- EXAM 25 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 12/37<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 45 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:41:32.918Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following describes the major benefit of verification early in the life cycle?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. It allows the identification of changes in user requirements. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. It facilitates timely set up of the test environment.</div><div class="opt correct">c. It reduces defect multiplication. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. It allows testers to become involved early in the project.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.1.1 và 1.2.3 chú ý vào từ "verification early" tìm sớm lỗi sẽ ko phát sinh nhiều vào trong các tài liệu khác</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">Even though a test that once revealed many defects is part of the regression suite, no new test cases have been created for the module under test in a long time. What test principle is the test team forgetting?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Absence-of-errors fallacy [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Defect clustering</div><div class="opt correct">c. Tests wear out [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Early testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.3. chú ý "no new test cases have been created"</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">Test objectives vary between projects and so must be stated in the test plan. Which one of the following test objectives might conflict with the proper tester mindset?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Show that the system works before we ship it. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Find as many defects as possible</div><div class="opt ">c. Reduce the overall level of product risk.</div><div class="opt ">d. Prevent defects through early involvement</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.3 Test ko chứng minh được hệ thống làm việc hay không vì thế mà "test objectives" và test mindset có thể bị mâu thuẫn với nhau</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following characterises the cost of faults?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. They are cheapest to find in the early development phases and the most expensive to fix in the latest test phases. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. They are easiest to find during system testing but the most expensive to fix then.</div><div class="opt ">c. Faults are cheapest to find in the early development phases but the most expensive to fix then.</div><div class="opt ">d. Although faults are most expensive to find during early development phases, they are cheapest to fix then.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.1.1 đặc điểm của chi phí về lỗi?</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which activity in the Fundamental Test Process creates test suites for efficient test execution?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Implementation and execution [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Analysis and design</div><div class="opt ">c. Planning and control</div><div class="opt ">d. Test closure</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.1 chú ý "creates test suites"</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">The list below (a to e) describes one major task for each of the five main activities of the fundamental test process. Which option (A to D) places the tasks in the correct order, by time? a) Create bi-directional traceability between test basis and test cases. b) Check test logs against exit criteria. c) Define the objectives of testing. d) Check planned deliverables have been delivered. e) Comparing actual results with expected results.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. a, c, b, e, d [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. c, a, d, e, b</div><div class="opt correct">c. c, a, e, b, d [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. d, a, c, b, e</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4.1 Thứ tự nào diễn ra là đúng? chọn c là task của test plan, a là của test design, e là test execution, b là evaluate exit criteria trong giai đoạn chạy test, d là của test completion</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following list contains only non-functional tests?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Interoperability (compatibility) testing, System testing, performance testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Load testing, stress testing, component testing, portability testing</div><div class="opt correct">c. Load testing, stress testing, reliability testing, performance testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Load testing, stress testing, component testing, portability testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 chỉ có B mới chứa các loại test types thuộc non-functional</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Acceptance testing means</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing performed on a single stand [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing after changes have been made to ensure that no unwanted changes were introduced</div><div class="opt correct">c. Testing to ensure that the system meets the needs of the organization and end user. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Users test the application in the developers environment</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 mục tiêu của acceptance test là validate product</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Integration testing where all the system’s components being combined to form the system at once.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. System testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Component testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Incremental testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Big-bang testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 Kiểm thử tích hợp trong đó tất cả các thành phần của hệ thống được kết hợp để tạo thành hệ thống cùng một lúc? Integration test level có 2 chiến lược tích hợp, trong đó Big bang= merge code</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Alpha testing is</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. post-release testing by end user representatives at the developer’s site. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. the first testing that is performed.</div><div class="opt correct">c. pre-release testing by end user representatives at the developer’s site. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. pre-release testing by end user representatives at their sites.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 chọn C, còn D là của Beta test, A sai vì post-release là sau release rồi, B thì sai hoàn toàn</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">An important benefit of code inspections is that they</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. enable the code to be tested before the execution environment is ready. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. can be performed by the person who wrote the code.</div><div class="opt ">c. can be performed by inexperienced staff.</div><div class="opt ">d. are cheap to perform.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.2, chính là lợi ích của static testing ( inspection là hình thức của review). B và C sai vì inspection review thì phải đc thực hiện bởi các reviewer có kinh nghiệm, ko phải là tác giả của code. Lăn tăn giữa A và D. Với D thì rẻ ( cheap) chỉ khi thực hiện informal review mới là hình thức rẻ còn inspection thì đắt vì có sự tham gia của nhiều người nên loại D. Ý A lúc đầu mình hiểu sai, ý của A là việc review code inspection sớm giúp code có thể đc test ( ở đây là static test) trước khi môi trường sẵn sàng cho dynamic test</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements about reviews is true?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Reviews cannot be performed on user requirements specifications. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Reviews are the least effective way of testing code.</div><div class="opt ">c. Reviews are unlikely to find faults in test plans.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Reviews should be performed on specifications, code, and test plans. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.3 Review sử dụng cho mọi loại tài liệu</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Increasing the quality of the software, by better development methods, will affect the time needed for testing (the test phases) by</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. increasing test time [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. no change</div><div class="opt correct">c. reducing test time [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. can’t say</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.2, chú ý vào "better development methods" phương pháp phát triển tốt hơn thì phải giúp giảm thời gian và chi phí</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Which requirement is testable?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The tested application is portable. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Loading time of the tested web application is within 3 seconds. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. The critical part of the tested application has no fault.</div><div class="opt ">d. The tested application is user-friendly.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 Requirement nào đủ rõ ràng và chi tiết để test đc chọn B đủ chi tiết</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">Inspections can find all the following except?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Requirements that have been omitted from the design documents [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Spelling and grammar faults in the documents</div><div class="opt ">c. Variables not defined in the code</div><div class="opt correct">d. How much of the code has been covered [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.2 câu hỏi là Inspection tìm ra tất cả lỗi trừ cái nào sau đây. D là của dynamic test còn inspection là của static testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Arrive-and-Go airline wants to clarify its baggage handling policy, whilst maximizing revenues, and will introduce the following tariffs for all baggage per individual customer (weights are rounded up to the nearest 0.1Kg): The first 2Kg will be carried free of charge. The next 10 Kg will be carried for a flat charge of 
20.
