20.Anadditional15Kgwillbechargedatotalchargeof27. Luggage over this amount will be charged at $5 per Kg, up to a maximum of 150Kg per person. No passenger may take more that 150Kg with them. Which of the following would constitute boundary values for baggage weights in the price calculation?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1.9, 12.0, 14.9, 150.0 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 2.0, 9.9, 15.0, 26.9</div><div class="opt ">c. 0, 5.0, 10.0, 17.0</div><div class="opt correct">d. 2.0, 12.1, 27.0, 150.1 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a form of functional testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Boundary value analysis [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Usability testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Performance testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Security testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2. BCD đều là non functional</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Company ABC is going to provide their employees with a bonus which will be based on the employee’s length of service in the company. The bonus calculation will be zero if they have been with the company for less than two years, 10% of their salary for more than two but less than five years, and 25% for five to ten years, 35% for ten years or more. The interface will not allow a negative value to be input, but it will allow a zero to be input. How many equivalence partitions are needed to test the calculation of the bonus?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 4 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 2</div><div class="opt ">c. 3</div><div class="opt correct">d. 5 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Nó hỏi về EP là phân vùng tương đương để tính đc bonus: not allow a negative value nên có vùng &lt;0, 0 đến &lt;2, từ 2 đến &lt;5, từ 5 đến &lt;10, trên 10 năm, nên có 5 phân vùng</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">A wholesaler sells printer cartridges. The minimum order quantity is 5. There is a 20% discount for orders of 100 or more printer cartridges. You have been asked to prepare test cases using various values for the number of printer cartridges ordered. Which of the following groups contain three test inputs that would be generated using Boundary Value Analysis?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 5, 6, 20 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 4, 5, 99 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 4, 5, 80</div><div class="opt ">d. 1, 20, 0100</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is the most important difference between the metrics-based approach and the expert-based approach to test estimation?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. The metrics-based approach uses calculations from historical data while the expert based approach relies on team wisdom. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. The metrics-based approach can be used to verify an estimate created using the expert-based approach, but not vice versa</div><div class="opt ">c. The expert-based approach takes longer than the metrics-based approach.</div><div class="opt ">d. The metrics-based approach is more accurate than the expert-based approach.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.4 Điều nào sau đây là sự khác biệt quan trọng nhất giữa metrics-based và expert-based ? theo sách chọn A, còn các B C D đang so sánh 2 kỹ thuật này ko có căn cứ</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">How would you estimate the amount of re-testing likely to be required?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Metrics from previous similar projects [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Discussions with the development team</div><div class="opt ">c. Time allocated for regression testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. a &amp; b [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.4. Bạn ước tính effort cho re-test như thế nào? cần có a là metric based và b là expert based nên chọn D</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following benefits are MOST likely to be achieved by using test tools? i) Easy to access information about tests and testing. ii) Reduced maintenance of testware. iii) Easy and cheap to implement. iv) Greater consistency of tests.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. i and iii [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. i and iv [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. ii and iii</div><div class="opt ">d. ii and iv</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 6.2 Lợi ích nào sau đây có khả năng đạt được NHIỀU NHẤT khi sử dụng các công cụ kiểm tra? theo sách chọn i và iv</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">After a record of poor quality software releases (incorrect menu selection options, new features that do not work, users allowed to change security levels without administrator rights), you have been asked to review the test capability in your company. You have limited time to do the review before the next project, which type of testing would be MOST appropriate to review first?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Functional testing. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Non-functional testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Performance testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Structural testing. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer chapter 2.3 Test type, Họ nói là thơi gian bị giới hạn thì cái test type nào phù hợp để review đầu tiên. Lúc đầu mình thấy các lỗi họ đưa ra là thuộc về functional thì Nếu là câu hỏi là Run test cho loại nào đầu tiên thì tất nhiên chọn functional rồi, phần mô tả ko liên quan gì đến non-functional và performance cả. Nên loại C, D đi vì ko mô tả gì về performance hay security cũng ko phải nhé ( users allowed to change security levels without administrator rights -- cái này đang mô tả tính năng chứ ko phải security). Nhưng câu hỏi là review cái nào phừ hợp ( chứ nó ko hỏi chạy test) nên giữa A và D thì thấy review nên dùng Whitebox test sẽ nhanh hơn, tập trung vào phần code đang sai</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Testing and Debugging are key activities in the software development lifecycle. Which of the following are DEBUGGING activities? a) Designing tests to find failures. b) Locating the cause of failures. c) Analysing and fixing the defects. d) Executing tests to show failures.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. a and d. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. a and b.</div><div class="opt correct">c. b and c. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. c and d.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.1.2 Kiểm tra và gỡ lỗi là các hoạt động chính trong vòng đời phát triển phần mềm. Hoạt động nào sau đây là hoạt động DEBUGGING? chọn b c</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">Testing and Debugging are key activities in the software development lifecycle. Which of the following are TESTING activities? a) Designing tests to find failures. b) Locating the cause of failures. c) Analysing and fixing the defects. d) Executing tests to show failures.</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. a and d [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. a and b.</div><div class="opt ">c. b and c.</div><div class="opt ">d. c and d.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.1.2 Kiểm tra và gỡ lỗi là các hoạt động chính trong vòng đời phát triển phần mềm. Hoạt động nào sau đây là hoạt động THỬ NGHIỆM? chọn a, d là của testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following options BEST explains the "Tests wear out" principle of testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. If we do not regularly review and revise our tests, we’ll stop finding defects. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Repeatedly running a set of tests will ensure that a system is defect free.</div><div class="opt ">c. Defects are, paradoxically, often contained in a small number of modules.</div><div class="opt ">d. Testing, like spraying pesticide, is an effective bug/defect removal activity</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.3. chọn A vì "not regularly review and revise our tests" Test case không đc review và chỉnh sửa thường xuyên</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement about Static Testing is TRUE?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Static testing can be applied to any work product that participants know how to read and understand. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Static testing must only be applied to final work products that have been signed off.</div><div class="opt ">c. Static testing must be conducted by users of the product being tested.</div><div class="opt ">d. Static testing executes the code to verify the functionality is as expected.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.1 Cái nào đúng về Static testing? chọn A đúng, loại B vì "must only be applied to final work products" chỉ áp dụng trên sản phẩm cuối cùng, C sai vì "conducted by users", D sai vì "Static testing executes the code"</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">What does the term “Tests wear out” refer to?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The phenomena where a piece of code that has a lot of bugs is likely to have more hidden, yet unfound bugs [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The decreasing efficiency of debugging when done in code that has many bugs</div><div class="opt correct">c. Reduced effectiveness of test cases that are repeated and focused on the same scenarios [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The redundancy of testing the same objects in both black and white box techniques</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.3 Thuật ngữ “Thử nghiệm hao mòn” ám chỉ điều gì? chú ý chọn C vì "Repeated and focused on the same scenarios"</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following test techniques is structure-based?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Control flow testing [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Use case testing</div><div class="opt ">c. State transition testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Decision table testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.3.4 Kỹ thuật kiểm thử nào sau đây dựa trên cấu trúc? xem bảng summary của white box test</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Pair programming is done with developer and tester pairing together [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Pair programming is an alternative</div><div class="opt ">c. Pair programming is used usually in waterfall model</div><div class="opt correct">d. Pair programming is, among other things, an informal review method [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.2.3 review types (Pair programming là pair review)</div><h2>Cau hoi 31</h2><div class="qtext">In foundation level syllabus you will find the main basic principles of testing. Which of the following sentences describes one of these basic principles?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Complete testing of software is attainable if you have enough resources and test tools [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. For a software system, it is not possible, under normal conditions, to test all input and output combinations [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. A goal of testing is to show that the software is defect free</div><div class="opt ">d. With automated testing you can make statements with more confidence about the quality of a product than with manual testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.3 Câu nào sau đây mô tả một trong những nguyên tắc cơ bản này? chú ý vào "it is not possible" chọn B là nguyên lý "2. Exhaustive testing is impossible". Loại A vì nó bảo test toàn bộ phần mềm có thể đạt đc nếu bạn có đủ resource và tools, Loại C vì nó bảo mục đích của test là để chứng minh phần mềm ko có lỗi, Loại D vì dịch ra câu này thì ko có trong nguyên lý " với automation test bạn khẳng định đc là tự tin hơn về chất lượng của sản phầm so với manual test"</div><h2>Cau hoi 32</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an example of black-box dynamic testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Code inspection [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Checking memory leaks for a program by executing it</div><div class="opt correct">c. Functional Testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Coverage analysis</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.1.1 A là của static test, B là dynamic analysis bởi tool tìm ra lỗi về bộ nhớ, D là của white box test, còn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 33</h2><div class="qtext">Where and by whom is Beta testing normally performed?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. By customers or potential customers at their own locations [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. By an independent test team at the developing organization’s location</div><div class="opt ">c. At the developing organization’s site, but not by the developing team</div><div class="opt ">d. By customers or potential customers at the developing organization’s site</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 chọn A là định nghĩa của Beta test, loại C D vì là định nghĩa của Alpha test, loại B vì "an independent test team" là đội dự án ko phải bên KH</div><h2>Cau hoi 34</h2><div class="qtext">When testing a mission critical system, a high coverage should be achieved. Which of the following techniques should be implemented as a structural based coverage technique in order to achieve the highest coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. multiple condition coverage [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. decision table</div><div class="opt ">c. use case testing</div><div class="opt ">d. statement coverage</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.3.4 nhìn vào bảng Summary của white box test sẽ thấy mức độ coverage cao nhất là A, B C loại vì của black box test, D thấp nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 35</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT a valid objective of testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Ensuring required coverage of a test object [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Investigating and fixing defects in the software under test [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Gaining confidence that the system is fit-for-purpose</div><div class="opt ">d. Providing information for stakeholders' decision making</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.1.1 chọn B vì là của debug</div><h2>Cau hoi 36</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a defect that is more likely to be found by a static analysis tool than by other testing techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Omission of a major requirement [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Inadequate decision coverage</div><div class="opt ">c. Component memory leakage</div><div class="opt correct">d. Variables that are not used improperly declared [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.3 lỗi tìm đc bới static analysis tool là chủ yếu trong code nên chọn D là 1 cái biến chưa được khai báo, C loại vì lỗi memory leakage tìm đc bởi dynamic analysis tool, B loại vì decision coverage là lỗi của white box test, A loại vì là lỗi bởi review tìm đc</div><h2>Cau hoi 37</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following type of defect would NOT be typically found by using a static analysis tool?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A variable is defined but is then not used [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. A variable is used in a calculation before it is defined</div><div class="opt correct">c. A variable has the wrong numeric value passed into it [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. A variable is used but not declared</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.3, tất cả các lỗi đều nằm trong code nhưng chọn C vì nó quá cụ thể về "the wrong numeric value" không phải lúc nào giá trị test cũng là dạng số</div></body></html>